{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And He formed.</b> By the power of the luminaries. And וייצר is among the verbs whose first root letter is yod in the kal binyan, like וייקץ נח (Genesis 9:24)." "The sense of באפיו: through them a person lives, for they expel the hot air from the heat of the heart, and bring in cooler air." "The sense of לנפש חיה: that he walked immediately like the animals, and not like infants."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved the reference to the verb's morphology from context; the first root letter (פ\"א) refers to the פ״י פעל position.", 1 "Reading אהר as a variant/defective form of אויר קריר or similar; the text may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:46.602789225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}